{number: 94}
{title: Great Is Thy Faithfulness}
{key: Eb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Eb] Great is Thy faithfulness, [Ab] O God my Father,
[Bb7] There is no shadow of [Eb] turning with Thee;
Thou [Eb] changest not, Thy com-[Ab] passions they fail not;
As [F7] Thou hast been Thou for-[Bb7] ever wilt be.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Bb7] Great is Thy faithfulness! [Eb] Great is Thy faithfulness!
[Bb7] Morning by morning new [Eb] mercies I see;
All [Eb] I have needed Thy [Ab] hand hath provided,
[Eb] Great is Thy faithfulness, [Bb7] Lord, unto [Eb] me!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Eb] Summer and winter, and [Ab] springtime and harvest,
[Bb7] Sun, moon and stars in their [Eb] courses above,
Join [Eb] with all nature in [Ab] manifold witness
To [F7] Thy great faithfulness, [Bb7] mercy and love.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Eb] Pardon for sin and a [Ab] peace that endureth,
[Bb7] Thine own dear presence to [Eb] cheer and to guide;
Strength [Eb] for today and bright [Ab] hope for tomorrow,
Bless-[F7] ings all mine, with ten [Bb7] thousand beside!
{end_of_verse}
